{
  "requirement": "The requirements index MUST show each requirement's evidence state as Valid, Missing, Determination false, FIXME, or Invalid. Valid MUST mean its determination is true and its record passes the same evidence and reference coverage checks as `habeas::validate()`. A false or FIXME determination MUST have its distinct state when the record passes all other checks. The FIXME state MUST pass validation while retaining its distinct label. Malformed or stale evidence MUST remain Invalid regardless of its determination. Each detail page MUST show any validation findings.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "## Judgment: requirements.index.state is satisfied\n\n### Implementation (`src/index.rs`)\n\n- **State derivation.** `LoadedDetailEvidence::load` (l.154–209) does the work.\n  - It takes the repository-wide `EvidenceReport` produced by `inspect_repository`. That is the same inspection `habeas::validate()` runs: schema, stale text and inputs, dependencies, `{impl}`/`{test}` reference coverage (`validate_references`), and the example-test check.\n  - It keeps the errors whose prefix is `evidence/<name>.json:`. Per-record coverage and staleness errors are all emitted with that prefix, e.g. \"no input covers…\", \"requirement text changed\", \"outline input changed\", and \"has a true determination but no {test} reference\".\n  - Missing: the file is absent. The \"missing for requirement\" finding is still shown.\n  - No findings: True maps to Valid, False to Determination false, and FIXME to FIXME. An unparsable determination maps to Invalid.\n  - With findings: the state is Determination false only if every finding is the \"determination is false\" error. Anything else is Invalid. So stale or malformed evidence stays Invalid whatever the determination, and FIXME with any finding is Invalid.\n  - FIXME produces no validation error in `validate_evidence_file`, so it passes validation while keeping its own label.\n- **Labels.** `EvidenceState::label` (l.240) gives exactly Valid / Missing / Determination false / FIXME / Invalid.\n- **Index table.** `DetailPlan::populate` (l.331) puts `evidence.state().label()` in each index row.\n- **Detail pages.** `render_detail_sections` (l.660) renders the state badge. When `errors` is non-empty it adds a \"Validation findings\" section, so each detail page shows its findings.\n- **Minor points.**\n  - `EvidenceState::color` is marked `{impl}`. No definition specifies colors, but they only style the required state badge, so I treat this as harmless.\n  - The enum itself is marked only `{cite}`. Its behavior is carried by the `{impl}`-marked `label` and `load`, so this is not a material marking gap.\n  - Rust-function-coverage findings are repository-wide, not tied to one evidence record, so they are not attached to individual states. They are not an evidence or reference-coverage check on the record.\n\n### Tests\n\n- `index_shows_evidence_states_and_links_generated_chapters` (src/index.rs l.1041) checks the index rows for Valid, Determination false, Missing, and Invalid. It covers stale requirement text and an uncovered `{impl}` reference. It also checks the badge on the Valid page and the \"requirement text changed\" finding on the stale page.\n- `findings_make_false_and_fixme_records_invalid` (l.1507) covers the boundaries:\n  - a false record that is clean, stale, malformed, or has an uncovered reference;\n  - a FIXME record that is clean or stale;\n  - that \"Validation findings\" appears on every page except the clean FIXME one.\n- `tests/outcomes.rs`:\n  - `malformed_fixme_is_invalid_and_reports_the_required_shape` covers a malformed FIXME, which is Invalid.\n  - `fixme_does_not_hide_stale_inputs_or_uncovered_references` covers a FIXME with a stale input or an uncovered reference, which is Invalid.\n  - `valid_fixme_remains_visible_in_status_info_and_book` covers a clean FIXME. It shows FIXME in the index and `evidence-FIXME` on the detail page, and validation passes.\n\nTogether these cover each state, the false and FIXME \"all other checks pass\" cases, the \"Invalid regardless of determination\" cases (stale text, stale input, malformed record, uncovered reference), and findings on detail pages. No FIXME-acknowledged gaps remain.",
  "inputs": [
